  "qualification": "Source-only explicit public consumer-capable account attachment. The old producer-only setter/rejection and NULL-account behavior remain, while a closed attachment value preserves account/profile through configuration clones and failure and a public C consumer sibling reuses unchanged common native initialization/cleanup. The existing AccountedNativePtr client/queue/event chain and independent Metadata owner retain the actual monitor. Receive/handshake denial follows ordinary native broker error/reconnect/backoff with existing suppression; fatal state remains separate. Real uncompressed fetch/retained consumer and Metadata source fixtures exercise native owner lifetime. Decompression/shadow buffers, individual fetch/error ops and strings, request/list/aborted-transaction state, native construction/thread/queue and other allocation classes are outside this ceiling. Connect/log/DLQ activation and compatible fetch/receive/capacity policy are separate call-site work; no whole-consumer/Java/runtime/Phase 2 closure is claimed."
